{"uid":"modules/verb_catalog.py","name":"verb_catalog.py","qualname":"modules/verb_catalog.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/verb_catalog.py","line":1,"end_line":569,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Operator-owned YAML catalog of every routable shell verb.","description":"The autonomous loop historically routed only the built-in ``auto_*``\nverbs; every other cmd2 command was reachable only when the text of an\nintent literally named it. This module flips the model: the shell\ncatalogue is discovered once (``cli/command_index.json`` plus the same\n``do_*`` scan the CLI bridge uses), materialised as ``config/verbs.yaml``\nand every entry starts disabled unless it is enabled today.\n\nOwnership split (SOLID):\n\n- this module owns discovery, YAML persistence and catalog queries;\n- ``modules/orchestrator_config`` keeps owning the merged view the loop\n  reads, so the TUI, the API and the planner see one truth;\n- operator toggles live in ``config/verbs.yaml`` (versioned, diffable),\n  payload overrides keep working for advanced verb fields.\n\nA missing, invalid or oversized YAML never raises into the loop: the\ncatalog degrades to \"no catalog entries\" and routing falls back to the\nbuilt-in verb set only.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/verb_catalog.py::DEFAULT_CATALOG_PATH","modules/verb_catalog.py::DEFAULT_INDEX_PATH","modules/verb_catalog.py::BUILTIN_ENABLED_VERBS","modules/verb_catalog.py::VerbCatalogConfig","modules/verb_catalog.py::index_commands","modules/verb_catalog.py::validate_catalog","modules/verb_catalog.py::load","modules/verb_catalog.py::entries","modules/verb_catalog.py::catalog_enabled","modules/verb_catalog.py::set_enabled","modules/verb_catalog.py::sync","modules/verb_catalog.py::stats","modules/verb_catalog.py::search"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
